    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/541194/senior-officer-policy-contracts": {
      "title": "Senior Officer, Policy & Contracts",
      "description": "Senior Officer, Policy & Contracts Apply now Job no: 541194 Work type: Full Time Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Student Services, Governance, Policy & Compliance Employment Type: Full Time (35 hours per week) Duration: 18 month Fixed Term Contract Remuneration: Level 7 from $118k + 17% superannuation & leave loading Location:  Kensington NSW (Hybrid Working Arrangements) Why your role matters The Senior Officer, Policy & Contracts supports the delivery of employability, work-integrated learning and industry engagement initiatives by providing professional advice, drafting and administering contracts, implementing policy and compliance requirements, and engaging with key stakeholders. Working closely with Faculties, Divisions and external partners, the role facilitates effective contracting, governance and operational outcomes, while providing advice on legislative, regulatory, policy and strategic matters relevant to employability and work-integrated learning. The role also manages complex case escalations from Faculties and Divisions and reports to the Lead, Policy & Contracts within the Employability team in the Pro Vice-Chancellor Student Success Portfolio. Specific accountabilities include: In collaboration with the Lead, Policy & Contracts and the UNSW Legal, Insurance and Risk teams provide professional advice and support on policy, procedural and contractual matters relating to employability, work integrated learning and industry engagement activities. Coordinate the drafting, review, amending and negotiation of contracts and related documentation. Assist in the interpretation and implementation of legislative, regulatory and institutional policy requirements relevant to employability, work integrated learning and industry engagement activities. Project manages system reviews and new system development, liaising with stakeholders for consultation and implementation processes. Support and coordinate the development, implementation and review of policies, procedures and guidance materials About You: Relevant tertiary qualification with subsequent relevant experience or equivalent competence gained through any combination of education, training, and experience. A Bachelor of Laws or Juris Doctor is desirable. Demonstrated experience in policy administration, contract management including experience preparing, reviewing and coordinating contractual and policy documentation. Demonstrated ability to provide professional advice and recommendations within established policy frameworks. Strong stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience preparing reports, briefing papers and correspondence. Proven organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes within agreed timeframes. An understanding of and commitment to UNSW’s aims, objectives and values in action, together with relevant policies and guidelines. For further details on role responsibilities and skills & experience required, refer to the position description found under the position listing on Jobs@UNSW . Benefits and Culture: People are at the core of everything we do. We recognise it is the contributions of our staff who make UNSW one of the best universities in Australia and the world. Our benefits include: Flexible working options. Career development opportunities. 17% Superannuation contributions and additional leave loading payments. Additional 3 days of leave over Christmas period. Discounts and entitlements (retail, education, fitness). For further details on the benefits, please visit https://www.jobs.unsw.edu.au/lifestyle-benefits Pre-Employment Checks As part of our recruitment process candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening, which may include reference checks, qualification verification, right-to-work verification, and criminal history screening where relevant to the role. How to Apply: Submit your CV & Cover Letter addressing your suitability to the role in relation to the selection criteria (in approximately 2 pages) before 11.55pm Sunday 27 September 2026. Please note: Sponsorship is not available for this role, valid Australian working rights are required on application. Job queries contact: Chloe Gane, Talent Acquisition Consultant E: chloe.gane@unsw.edu.au (applications to the address cannot be accepted, please apply online) UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Position Description Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 27 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/541735/senior-business-analyst-hr-data-processes": {
      "title": "Senior Business Analyst, HR Data Processes",
      "description": "Senior Business Analyst, HR Data Processes Apply now Job no: 541735 Work type: Full Time Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Analyst Employment Type: Full time, 2-year Fixed Term position. Remuneration: Level 9 – from $153,933 + 17% superannuation. Location: Kensington, NSW (Full time on-site role) About the Role We are seeking an experienced Senior Business Analyst to lead HR data processes and legacy system cleanup as part of an upcoming system conversion. In this role, you will work closely with the Program Manager and data stakeholders to gain an in-depth understanding of business strategy, processes, services, and roadmaps, while documenting the capabilities required to address key business challenges. The successful applicant will possess: Proven experience in HR data migration, legacy system decommissioning, and data cleansing operations Demonstrated expertise in mapping HR processes, workflows, and data structures from end to end Strong stakeholder management skills to align technical data teams with HR business objectives A track record of translating complex business requirements into clear functional documentation and technical specifications Support leadership in optimising the way in which the Integration sub domain work, including documentation of business requirements, Mapping of data integration and services, practices, organisation, and resourcing to promote team dynamics and opportunities for continuous improvement. Oversee and finalise effective communications with key stakeholders, both internal and external and provide influential input with stakeholders to achieve business outcomes. Provide leadership, guidance, advice and business analysis quality assurance to the team assigned to the project which the Business Analyst has a role. Identify and evaluate business requirements for one or more systems or process areas. Investigate, analyse and document business processes and the underlying business model for a system or process area. Collaborate closely with developers, Architects and Business SMEs to implement the requirements, provide necessary guidance to testers during QA process. Build and execute product functional test plans prior to release to end-users. Develop operational and user guides and develop and deliver end-user training. About You Relevant tertiary qualification combined with subsequent HR systems experience, or equivalent competence gained through education, training, and professional background. At least 5 years of functional experience as a business analyst, functional consultant, or systems specialist focusing on HR data migrations, system implementations, and legacy data cleanup in a large, complex organisation—ideally within higher education. Extensive knowledge of and experience across a range of application development methodologies, including Agile, Waterfall, Lean, and Rapid Application Development. Proven experience in business case preparation, workload estimation, and project costing tailored to large-scale data and systems transformations. High-level competency in professional business analysis techniques and methods, such as Use Case Analysis and UML, specifically applied to HR data workflows and integration processes. Well-developed proficiency in standard office applications, diagramming tools like Visio, and collaboration platforms such as JIRA and Confluence. Sound consultation, influencing, and negotiation skills to engage effectively with diverse HR and technical stakeholders, ensuring alignment during data cleanup and migration. Comprehensive analytical and problem-solving skills to navigate complex legacy HR datasets, exercise initiative, and develop robust data quality solutions. Advanced written and verbal communication skills, with a high level of attention to detail for process maps, functional specifications, and migration documentation. For further information on the role & responsibilities, please refer to the Position Description How to Apply: Submit your CV & cover letter detailing your interest and suitability for the job (as per the skills & experience bullet points in the job description ) before Sunday 20 September by 11:55pm. Please note: Sponsorship is not available for this role, valid Australian working rights are required on application. UNSW Benefits and Culture: People are at the core of everything we do. We recognise it is the contributions of our staff who make UNSW one of the best universities in Australia and the world. Our benefits include: Flexible Working Options (work from home, flexible hours etc) Additional 3 days leave during December festive period. Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% Superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice. Discounts and entitlements (retail, education, fitness passport) UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Position Description Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 20 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/541745/multiple-permanent-teaching-roles-canberra-school-of-professional-studies": {
      "title": "Multiple Permanent Teaching Roles, Canberra School of Professional Studies",
      "description": "Multiple Permanent Teaching Roles, Canberra School of Professional Studies Apply now Job no: 541745 Work type: Full Time Location: Canberra, ACT Categories: Senior Lecturer, Lecturer, Associate Lecturer Senior Lecturer in AI and Digital Transformation and Application (Balanced) Associate Lecturer/ Lecturer in Information Management, Data Science and Analytics (EF) Lecturer in Software Engineering, Web Security and Cyber Security/Cyber Operations (EF) Senior Lecturer in Applied Cyber Security (Balanced) Senior Lecturer in Cyber Security Applications, Leadership, AI and Security Management (EF) Lecturer in Applied Digital Technology (EF) Employment type: Full-time (35 hours) Duration: Continuing Remuneration: Level A (Associate Lecturer) from $ 95,036, Level B (Lecturer) from $ 133,065, Level C (Senior Lecturer) from $ 161,619 + leave loading + 17% super Location : UNSW Canberra, City Campus Work rights required: Visa sponsorship and relocation is not available for this position. Candidates must hold full rights to work in Australia to be considered. About UNSW Canberra University of New South Wales (UNSW) in Canberra has multiple locations in the Nation’s Capital. UNSW Canberra distinguishes itself from other institutions through its commitment to being thoughtful, practical, and purposeful in all endeavours. This combined approach is integral to the university's impact and contributes to its recognition as Australia’s No 1 University and ranked 19 th in the world. We are a proud member of Australia's esteemed Group of Eight. Why Your Role Matters: At Canberra School of Professional Studies , security is our default lens of operation. Emerging technologies are our tools of operation. Professional application of secure technologies in different professional contexts is our specialisation. We are made up of innovative academics and professionals with educational excellence and learner engagement, working in cutting edge research with strong industry engagement and experience. We are agile and nimble. We work in co-creative and co-located spaces with cutting edge industries and launch partners. We do things differently, think differently and challenge business as usual. We are not bogged down by bureaucracy. We collaborate to build intellectual capital and fertilise ideas. We produce professionals, upskill existing ones, and engender lifelong learning to address future skills challenges. Join us at this exciting stage of growth as we build a fresh and innovative academic school. We are seeking multiple academics who are passionate about teaching, research, industry engagement and student success, and who are eager to contribute to the development of a dynamic and emerging academic community. This is a unique opportunity to help shape the school's future, influence curriculum design, and establish a strong culture of academic excellence. Please see the six position descriptions for further information on these roles. Benefits and Culture: UNSW is committed to helping staff balance work-life responsibilities, by providing access to high-quality services, facilities, and flexible work and leave arrangements. Flexible working options (work from home, flexible hours etc) Additional three days leave during December festive period Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice UNSW-wide strategy to focus on Healthy Body, Healthy Mind, Healthy Places and Healthy Culture. You can learn more about our Benefits and Culture at Lifestyle & Benefits UNSW Eligibility: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold rights to work in Australia to be considered for this position. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. As part of our recruitment process candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening, which may include reference checks, qualification verification, right-to-work verification, and criminal history screening where relevant to the role. How to Apply: Make each day matter with a meaningful career at UNSW. Submit your application online before Monday 5 October 2026 at 11:30pm , including your CV and a 1–2-page cover letter addressing the required skills and experience outlined in the position description. In order to view the position description, please ensure that you allow pop-ups for https://www.jobs.unsw.edu.au Get in Touch: For role-related queries please contact: csps.cbr@unsw.edu.au For recruitment process-related queries please contact: Holly Whale – Talent Acquisition Partner h.whale@unsw.edu.au Applications cannot be accepted if sent directly to the contact listed. Find out more about the lifestyle and benefits when working with UNSW For further information about UNSW Canberra, please visit: UNSW Canberra For further information on living in Canberra, please visit: Living in Canberra UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Position Description Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 05 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/541963/associate-lecturer-in-it-project-management-lecturer-in-it-project-governance-and-security": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in IT Project Management & Lecturer in IT Project Governance and Security",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer in IT Project Management & Lecturer in IT Project Governance and Security Apply now Job no: 541963 Work type: Full Time Location: Canberra, ACT Categories: Lecturer, Associate Lecturer Associate Lecturer in IT Project Management (Level A), UNSW Canberra Lecturer in IT Project Governance and Security (Level B), UNSW Canberra Employment type: Fixed-term contracts, education-focused, full-time 35 hours Duration: 2 years (ideally to start by early 2027) Remuneration: Level A from $95,036 / Level B from $133,065 + leave loading + 17% super Location : UNSW Canberra, City Campus Work rights required: Visa sponsorship and relocation is not available for this position. Candidates must hold full rights to work in Australia to be considered. About UNSW Canberra University of New South Wales (UNSW) in Canberra has multiple locations in the Nation’s Capital. UNSW Canberra distinguishes itself from other institutions through its commitment to being thoughtful, practical, and purposeful in all endeavours. This combined approach is integral to the university's impact and contributes to its recognition as Australia’s No 1 University and ranked 19 th in the world. We are a proud member of Australia's esteemed Group of Eight. Why Your Role Matters: At Canberra School of Professional Studies , security is our default lens of operation. Emerging technologies are our tools of operation. Professional application of secure technologies in different professional contexts is our specialisation. We are made up of innovative academics and professionals with educational excellence and learner engagement, working in cutting edge research with strong industry engagement and experience. We are agile and nimble. We work in co-creative and co-located spaces with cutting edge industries and launch partners. We do things differently, think differently and challenge business as usual. We are not bogged down by bureaucracy. We collaborate to build intellectual capital and fertilise ideas. We produce professionals, upskill existing ones, and engender lifelong learning to address future skills challenges. Join us at this exciting stage of growth as we build a fresh and innovative academic school. We are seeking multiple academics who are passionate about teaching, research, industry engagement and student success, and who are eager to contribute to the development of a dynamic and emerging academic community. This is a unique opportunity to help shape the school's future, influence curriculum design, and establish a strong culture of academic excellence. Please see the two position descriptions for further information on these roles. Benefits and Culture: UNSW is committed to helping staff balance work-life responsibilities, by providing access to high-quality services, facilities, and flexible work and leave arrangements. Flexible working options (work from home, flexible hours etc) Additional three days leave during December festive period Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice UNSW-wide strategy to focus on Healthy Body, Healthy Mind, Healthy Places and Healthy Culture. You can learn more about our Benefits and Culture at Lifestyle & Benefits UNSW Eligibility: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold rights to work in Australia to be considered for this position. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. As part of our recruitment process candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening, which may include reference checks, qualification verification, right-to-work verification, and criminal history screening where relevant to the role. How to Apply: Make each day matter with a meaningful career at UNSW. Submit your application online before Monday 5 October 2026 at 11:30pm , including your CV and a 1–2-page cover letter addressing the required skills and experience outlined in the position description. In order to view the position description, please ensure that you allow pop-ups for https://www.jobs.unsw.edu.au Get in Touch: For role-related queries please contact: csps.cbr@unsw.edu.au For recruitment process-related queries please contact: Holly Whale – Talent Acquisition Partner h.whale@unsw.edu.au Applications cannot be accepted if sent directly to the contact listed. Find out more about the lifestyle and benefits when working with UNSW For further information about UNSW Canberra, please visit: UNSW Canberra For further information on living in Canberra, please visit: Living in Canberra UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Position Description Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 05 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
